{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1100,
    "dDurationMs": 733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "New York."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1833,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Independent Rent Guidelines Board\njust froze the rent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4600,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means\nif you're one of the more than 2"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6400,
    "dDurationMs": 2266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million New Yorkers\nwho lives in a rent stabilized apartment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8666,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your rent is going to be frozen next year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11900,
    "dDurationMs": 700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12600,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "New York, but also Dublin, Barcelona,\nBerlin, Amsterdam and Paris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16600,
    "dDurationMs": 4733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of these increasingly unaffordable\ncities, especially for regular people,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21333,
    "dDurationMs": 3467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have recently introduced\nor tightened rent controls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And people just love it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27600,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it makes total sense, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29500,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you live in these cities,\nyou know that rent can easily half,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34500,
    "dDurationMs": 1766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if not more, of your paycheck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36266,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, landlords are often\nunresponsive, irresponsible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40300,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and yet all too eager to jack up the rent\nwhenever they can."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45400,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So no wonder that even in polarized\nAmerica, rent controls are something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50200,
    "dDurationMs": 5433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that both liberals and most conservatives\nthe red dots support."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55933,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right,\neverybody loves rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59100,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except one\nparticularly annoying group of people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62700,
    "dDurationMs": 2233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economists agree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64933,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a 2012 US panel of prominent\neconomists,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68300,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only 2% agreed that rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72433,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have a positive impact on the amount\nand quality of affordable rental housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78100,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2%? Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80000,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even left wing economists\nlike Emmanuel Sys or Right Chetty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83633,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think rent controls\nare generally a bad idea."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86866,
    "dDurationMs": 1367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what's going on here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88233,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are economists just out of touch\nwith how regular people live,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92066,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or are they so neoliberal brainwashed\nthat they'll instinctively oppose"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96666,
    "dDurationMs": 3234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any government intervention\nanywhere on principle?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99900,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101400,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economists are not so pro free\nmarkets everywhere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105233,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they are against government\nprice controls in general."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108600,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, there's a textbook case\nwhere almost all of them agree that price"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113200,
    "dDurationMs": 4066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "controls, similar to rent controls,\nare exactly the right tool for the job."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117600,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when do price controls\nactually make sense?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121300,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer can be summarized\nin just one single word monopoly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126300,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, if you're the only seller\nof something people need,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129933,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have a super strong incentive\nto charge more and increase your profits"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134466,
    "dDurationMs": 4434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as much as you can, because your customers\nsimply have nowhere to go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139166,
    "dDurationMs": 2134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just think of the wire that brings"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141300,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you electricity\nor the pipe that brings you water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145133,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In these cases,\nthere is no natural competition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148933,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there never will be\nbecause digging up every street to lay"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152866,
    "dDurationMs": 4134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a second pipe\nor wire would be insanely expensive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157133,
    "dDurationMs": 1133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And wasteful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158266,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, economists call\nthese types of markets natural monopolies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163033,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So wherever these networks are in private\nhands, economists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166866,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tend to advise governments to set a limit\nto what these monopolies can charge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172933,
    "dDurationMs": 2267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because once prices are capped"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175200,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and squeezing\ncustomers is no longer a viable option."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179100,
    "dDurationMs": 2833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only way left\nfor commercial enterprises to earn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181933,
    "dDurationMs": 5633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more money is either\ncost cutting or serving more people,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187700,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is both good for the company\nand for the people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191400,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So economists are not always\nagainst price controls, yet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195266,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are firmly against rent\ncontrols. Why?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199033,
    "dDurationMs": 2267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer is very simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201300,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Landlords are not monopolists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203800,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure, big investment funds with lots\nof housing in their portfolio do exist,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208300,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the rental ownership is far\nless concentrated than people think."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212233,
    "dDurationMs": 2567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, in Spain, a country\nwhere rent prices in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214800,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "major cities have skyrocketed\nin the last decade,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218700,
    "dDurationMs": 4366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two thirds of the rental units\nare in the hands of landlords"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223466,
    "dDurationMs": 3534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with just 1 or 2 houses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227333,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand,\nindividual landlords with ten units"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231100,
    "dDurationMs": 5233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or more only represent\n3.6% of Spain's rental market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236433,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And according to an investigation\nof the Bank of Spain, investment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240466,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funds only control\nabout 8% of the rental units."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243733,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is not just a Spanish thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247300,
    "dDurationMs": 5533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Germany, only about 13% of rental\napartments are owned by private companies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252833,
    "dDurationMs": 3267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which tend to hold large\nportfolios of housing units."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256266,
    "dDurationMs": 2067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, most apartments were actually owned"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258333,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by private individuals\nand community owners."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262133,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, in the US,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263133,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the Wall Street is buying up\nall the houses, the story is loudest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267300,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Census Bureau's latest surveys\nfind that investment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270866,
    "dDurationMs": 5434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trusts and corporations\nwith more than a thousand units owned less"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276300,
    "dDurationMs": 3766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than 2% of the single family"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280066,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rental market,\nwhile three quarters of them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283166,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are in hands of owners\nwith less than ten units."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287900,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So rental markets are the opposite\nof a natural monopoly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291033,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because there are just so many landlords\ncompeting for the best renters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296100,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And crucially,\nif a market is already competitive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299433,
    "dDurationMs": 4633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then prices should, in theory,\nbe as low as they can be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304500,
    "dDurationMs": 2666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure, landlords will still make a profit,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307166,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this should not be excessive\nfor one simple reason"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311433,
    "dDurationMs": 5367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if rents are too high,\nthis introduces a massive incentives"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316800,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for landlords to simply build more homes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321166,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for example by building on vacant land\nor by building larger structures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325400,
    "dDurationMs": 2633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in theory, landlords should on average"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328033,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be pretty good\nand not make too high profits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331100,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in theory, rent controls\nwill disturb a healthy market"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335100,
    "dDurationMs": 4766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore lead to all sorts\nof unintended bad consequences."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340366,
    "dDurationMs": 1634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But is that actually true?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because on this channel\nI have the following simple rule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345000,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, theory is nice,\nbut what really matters is evidence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349133,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what actually happens\nwhen rent controls are introduced?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353966,
    "dDurationMs": 2434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Luckily for us, economist  Konstantin Kholodilin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356400,
    "dDurationMs": 2833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "did the dirty work of tracking down\nessentially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359233,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every empirical study\non rent controls ever written."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "92 peer reviewed studies covering 36"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366400,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "countries from 1967 all the way to 2022."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370600,
    "dDurationMs": 4366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what did all of these studies\nfind about rent controls?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375333,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, let's state the obvious."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377233,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, rent control\npolicies do work in the sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381233,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they lower\nand they have a negative impact on rent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385766,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for tenants\nliving in rent controlled apartments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389333,
    "dDurationMs": 4733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "36 out of the 41 published studies\nfind that once rent controls are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394066,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "introduced, rents do indeed go down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398266,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But remember, the rental market\nisn't nothing like a natural monopoly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402533,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Small landlords do compete with each other\nto find renters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407100,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for example by investing in properties\nto make them more modern and attractive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411733,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you say the rent can only be\nthis high, you essentially interfere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416033,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with this market process and landlords\nreact in typically one of two ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421800,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, some landlords decide\nthat if they cannot rent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425200,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at market prices,\nthey would rather sell their properties."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429400,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course,\nthat's actually good news for buyers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432100,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they will have more options\navailable for them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434833,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indeed, most published studies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436233,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "find that rent controls\ntend to increase home ownership,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440400,
    "dDurationMs": 4366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but in the short term, every home\nsold to a buyer is, of course, a home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444900,
    "dDurationMs": 2033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All the way from renters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446933,
    "dDurationMs": 4867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, not surprisingly, nine out of the ten\npublished studies found that while home"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451800,
    "dDurationMs": 4633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ownership increases, the rental supply\nshrinks, goes down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456466,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And given that not everybody can\nor wants to get a mortgage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460866,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it means that people who cannot afford to\nbuy will find it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463933,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more and more difficult\nto actually find a rental apartment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468100,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand,\nbecause now everyone wants to be inside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471600,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these nice rent controlled apartments,\nof which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474733,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are fewer and fewer are left\nbecause landlords are selling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477866,
    "dDurationMs": 5434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Almost all studies find that rent controls\ngreatly decrease mobility."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483566,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, people\nwho would have otherwise moved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486733,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because for example,\nthey found work in another city,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489866,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they started earning more,\nso they wanted a bigger apartment,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493200,
    "dDurationMs": 4066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or they need a smaller apartment\nbecause their kids just move out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497700,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many of these will now not move\nbecause they fear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501266,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "losing their nice rent\ncontrolled apartment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504366,
    "dDurationMs": 4967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while rent controls may benefit renters\nthat were already in the city,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509333,
    "dDurationMs": 4567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they make life much harder for people\nthat need to move into a new city"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513900,
    "dDurationMs": 5366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the future, because fewer and fewer\napartments will be becoming available."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519600,
    "dDurationMs": 4633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because some are sold and many people\nstay in place for a long time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524833,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This will force new people\nto look where the rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527933,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do not reach, like, for example,\nnewly built homes which are sometimes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531900,
    "dDurationMs": 4166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exempt, or apartments\nin the next town over."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536233,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So of course, virtually every study finds\nthat while rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540600,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in major cities or neighborhoods\ncause rent to decline, there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543933,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they cause rents\nto go up in uncontrolled markets nearby."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548433,
    "dDurationMs": 5567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So concretely, if Mamdani introduces\nrent controls in New York City, is likely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554000,
    "dDurationMs": 6066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to drive up rent prices in New York,\nwhich is nearby, but it gets even worse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560100,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, some landlords sell their rent\ncontrolled properties and some do not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564300,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But those that do not still face\nlower rent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567433,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more and more people\nthat want to get into their apartment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570800,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what do many of them do?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572800,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, they simply stop investing\nin keeping their apartments nice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577533,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They become worse landlords\nin other words, when the government"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580966,
    "dDurationMs": 3434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reduced their income by capping rents,\nthey simply responded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584400,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by reducing their costs\nto protect their profits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587700,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indeed, out of the 13 published studies\nthat examined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590700,
    "dDurationMs": 4266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "housing quality\nafter rent controls, about 11 of them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594966,
    "dDurationMs": 4634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "find that house quality goes down\nafter rent controls are introduced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599733,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But perhaps most worrying of all,\nmost studies by far show"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604833,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that rent controls decrease\nnew construction of rental properties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609300,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because of course, they have become less\ninteresting to invest in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613600,
    "dDurationMs": 5366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, the real effect of rent\ncontrols is that a lucky group of insiders"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618966,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who already had a nice apartment\nget a lower rent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622966,
    "dDurationMs": 2434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And perhaps that really helps them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625400,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But many of them still pay for it\nbecause their landlords"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629033,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will maintain these properties less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631933,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And second, more importantly,\nperhaps every renter who just happened"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635900,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be not in a rent controlled apartment\nat the time of rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640366,
    "dDurationMs": 1834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being introduced, will find that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642200,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is increasingly difficult\nto live in these cities at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is why most economists\nbelieve rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650000,
    "dDurationMs": 5066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had a negative impact on the amount\nand quality of affordable rental housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655600,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, most economists do agree"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658533,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that rents in major\ncities are out of control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661933,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if rent controls are not the solution,\nwhat solution do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665900,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most economists actually agree\non to reduce out-of-control rents?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670033,
    "dDurationMs": 967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's very simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671000,
    "dDurationMs": 3066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just build more housing units."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674433,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, if cities like New York,\nDublin and Paris keep growing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678133,
    "dDurationMs": 2867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they will of course need more workers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681000,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more workers need more homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683900,
    "dDurationMs": 2833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the obvious solution to out-of-control\nrents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686733,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that mayors like Mamdani\nshould simply build more homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Otherwise,\nthey end up creating a shortage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694466,
    "dDurationMs": 4434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a shortage is what gives landlords\nthe power in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699466,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rent controls\nattack the symptom, increasing rents,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703433,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and while that does reduce rents,\nit simply changes the problem to increased"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708233,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scarcity and the year long waiting lists\nfor rent controlled apartments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, building more addresses"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716700,
    "dDurationMs": 5233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the problem directly the disease\nwhen tenants have options, landlords"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721933,
    "dDurationMs": 5567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will compete for them and rents fall\nwithout anyone capping any prices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727800,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A good example is Auckland, New Zealand's\nbiggest city."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731733,
    "dDurationMs": 5667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 2016, Auckland rezoned a large part\nof the city to allow higher density."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737400,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Building and construction\nabsolutely exploded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741866,
    "dDurationMs": 4534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while rents still went up,\nthey did so far"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746400,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less dramatically than in, for example,\nanother New Zealand city, Wellington."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751033,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically, if we correct for inflation,\nwe can see that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753933,
    "dDurationMs": 4567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Auckland's rent prices\nstabilized while Wellington's exploded."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758500,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now this is not just that\nthe free market fix everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761766,
    "dDurationMs": 3234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many economists agree\nthat public housing is important as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765233,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When 50 people show up\nto see an apartment, there are always"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768466,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some unlucky people\nthat sit at the back of the line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771700,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with very few prospects\nof being ever picked up by landlords,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775933,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such as, for example, single moms\nor young people without a college degree."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780100,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And these people may"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780900,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "literally end up on the street\nif rental apartments are too expensive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 785100,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if the market fails to offer enough,\nthe government should step in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789033,
    "dDurationMs": 1967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and offer more public housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791000,
    "dDurationMs": 4733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the answer most economists support\nis just build more houses of every kind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796000,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Market rate housing, public housing,\nsocial housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799600,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yes, even if you see developers\nbuilding mostly luxury towers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804700,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this still helps\neveryone else, even the poor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808266,
    "dDurationMs": 3534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through a process that economists\ncall filtering, which is similar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811800,
    "dDurationMs": 3766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to musical chairs,\nin which you will of move into new units,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815800,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "freeing up the older units\nthey vacate and the chain reaches down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820000,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the income ladder further\nthan you might think at first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823666,
    "dDurationMs": 5767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So cities that build more like Auckland\nwill become more affordable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829433,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compared to cities like Wellington\nthat do not build more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834100,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sounds simple right? Case\nclosed. No, not quite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837000,
    "dDurationMs": 4366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because if the answer is so obvious,\nwhy does almost no expensive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841366,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "city like New York actually do it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845033,
    "dDurationMs": 5067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer turns out to be that new\nconstruction is very unpopular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850100,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because, perhaps not very surprisingly,\nmost people do not think like economists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855166,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, in a recent experiment,\neconomists Elmendorf, Nall and Oklobdzija "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859200,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "asked thousands of Americans\na very simple question if your city"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863733,
    "dDurationMs": 4867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "suddenly gets a lot more houses,\nwhat would happen to prices and rent?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869100,
    "dDurationMs": 5366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, only a minority of people said\nprices or rents would actually fall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874700,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, a whopping 42 or 43% of people\nthought the opposite would happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879833,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More construction means higher prices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883133,
    "dDurationMs": 1167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is very strange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884300,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they do seem to understand\nthe basic logic of supply and demand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888200,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, when asked how supply\nchain problems in the market for new cars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892433,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so fewer new cars would affect the price\nof used cars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896900,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "86% of respondents correctly predicted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900366,
    "dDurationMs": 4767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there would be higher prices for cars\nif there were fewer cars available."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905266,
    "dDurationMs": 1267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it's very clear to people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906533,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that if you were, cars can be made,\nthen prices will go up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909900,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for some reason, housing\nis where the logic breaks down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913833,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when asked who is to blame\nfor high housing prices, most respondents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918233,
    "dDurationMs": 4767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pointed their finger squarely\nat developers and landlords,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923166,
    "dDurationMs": 3367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which, while a bit depressing given\nall the evidence that we've seen so far"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926533,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about rent controls, was also quite\nenlightening because it can fully explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930900,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why, despite so much evidence\nagainst rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934833,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in favor of simply building\nmore housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938100,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Politicians often choose rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941233,
    "dDurationMs": 5867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the much simpler and crucially,\nmuch more popular option."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947400,
    "dDurationMs": 5633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in conclusion, why do almost 90%\nof economists about rent controls?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 953200,
    "dDurationMs": 700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 953900,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The evidence from dozens of studies\nshows us that while rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 957233,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do work in lowering rents\nfor current renters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960566,
    "dDurationMs": 3134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they do not solve the underlying problem\na housing shortage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963966,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, they shift the problem\nfrom the current and future tenants"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968100,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to just future tenants\nthat were just unlucky not to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971900,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a rent controlled apartment at the time\nthat rent controls were introduced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976266,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, the experience of cities\nlike Auckland shows us very clearly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 980133,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that building\nmore homes will stabilize rents."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984066,
    "dDurationMs": 4334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, even if those are luxury homes,\nbecause that means rich"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "families will leave less luxury apartments\navailable for others."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993866,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But can't we just do both?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996566,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well,\nthe evidence seems to point the other way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999866,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Studies have found that one of the most\ndamaging effects of rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003966,
    "dDurationMs": 4934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that they actually reduce construction\nby making renting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008900,
    "dDurationMs": 4566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less interesting for landlords\nto invest in new housing units."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013800,
    "dDurationMs": 1966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet you could imagine that someone like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015766,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mamdani will announce a massive public\nhousing construction plan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019900,
    "dDurationMs": 4733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alongside rent controls,\nbut so far he has sent mixed signals on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024633,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just how committed he is to building\nmore at least market rate housing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029266,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only focusing on publicly subsidized,\npermanently affordable, union built,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033800,
    "dDurationMs": 4566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rent stabilized homes, which, thanks to\nits very narrow definition, that only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038366,
    "dDurationMs": 4834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few types of homes will be incredibly\ndifficult to build at scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043333,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet who knows, maybe he can do it anyway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047266,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those are my two legs. What do you think?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1049166,
    "dDurationMs": 1367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you think economists are right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050533,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to prefer building more over\nimposing rent controls?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053300,
    "dDurationMs": 2233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Given all the evidence that you've seen?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055533,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me know in the comments below."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057966,
    "dDurationMs": 3367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you want to dig deeper\ninto more analysis on what actually does"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061333,
    "dDurationMs": 1667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work to make housing more affordable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063000,
    "dDurationMs": 3366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I highly recommend\nyou check out the following three articles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066366,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from our advertising sponsor,\nThe Economist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069700,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, for a big picture view of Europe's\nhousing crunch, start with this piece on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073933,
    "dDurationMs": 1667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why renting a one bedroom apartment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075600,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Lisbon now costs\nmore than the average Portuguese salary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079733,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, for another example of policy to\nprotect the renters can make things worse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084200,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Check out this article."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1085800,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, check out The Economist's\nDeep Dive into the structural forces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089966,
    "dDurationMs": 3267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pushing rents\nhigher across the entire world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093266,
    "dDurationMs": 3367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As these examples show,\nThe Economist delivers insights"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096633,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that help you see the bigger picture\nand think for yourself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099833,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is why I almost always rely\non their analysis from my research,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103866,
    "dDurationMs": 2334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's why\nI highly recommend you subscribe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106200,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is actually now more interesting\nthan ever,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109966,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "given that they are offering a special 50%\nsummer discount if you follow our link."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116133,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether you prefer daily journalism\nin The Economist app,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1118900,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
